From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 20 Sep 2026 21:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rk3399-pinephone-pro: wire the WiFi host-wake
 interrupt

Without an out-of-band wake line brcmfmac offers no wake-on-WLAN at all,
so cfg80211 tears the association down on every suspend. On LuneOS that
costs a full reassociation on each resume and leaves the phone
unreachable while it sleeps: nothing that arrives over the air can wake
it, and its own logs show it simply absent from the network for as long
as it is suspended.

Measured on the phone before this change:

    # iw phy phy0 info | grep -i wowlan     (nothing)
    # iw phy phy0 wowlan enable magic-packet
    command failed: Operation not supported (-95)
    # ls /proc/device-tree/mmc@fe310000/wifi@1
    compatible  name  pinctrl-0  pinctrl-names  reg

There is no interrupt in the node, which is why the driver advertises
nothing: on SDIO brcmfmac only exposes WOWL when it has a host-wake
interrupt to arm.

The line itself is already described. The pinctrl group wifi_host_wake_l
muxes GPIO4_D0 for exactly this purpose and nothing else in the board
uses that pin, and the firmware on the device carries the matching
controls (wowl_gpio, wowl_gpiopol in brcmfmac43456-sdio.bin, fifteen
wowl variables in the 43455 image). Only the interrupt properties were
commented out, by 79f9c93f0bcb ("Disable interrupt GPIO for WiFi for the
Pinephone Pro"), because the OOB interrupt breaks dev-version boards and
firmware configurations that do not use it.

This board is not one of those: its firmware provides the GPIO wake
variables. Restore the three properties so the driver can offer
magic-packet wake, which LuneOS then arms automatically from its udev
helper.

If a unit does turn out to be an OOB-less one, the symptom is WiFi that
no longer associates, and the remedy is to drop this patch again.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board-specific; upstream disabled this
deliberately in 79f9c93f0bcb because it breaks dev-version boards and
firmware configurations without OOB interrupts]

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-pinephone-pro.dts | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-pinephone-pro.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-pinephone-pro.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-pinephone-pro.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3399-pinephone-pro.dts
@@ -1503,9 +1503,9 @@
 	brcmf: wifi@1 {
 		compatible = "brcm,bcm4329-fmac";
 		reg = <1>;
-		//interrupt-parent = <&gpio4>;
-		//interrupts = <RK_PD0 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
-		//interrupt-names = "host-wake";
+		interrupt-parent = <&gpio4>;
+		interrupts = <RK_PD0 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+		interrupt-names = "host-wake";
 		pinctrl-names = "default";
 		pinctrl-0 = <&wifi_host_wake_l>;
 	};
